{
  "comment": [
    "bleep.ProcessMemory.MacOs measures a process's phys_footprint and CPU time with proc_pid_rusage (and mach_timebase_info), through java.lang.foreign.",
    "It reaches java.lang.foreign by reflection (bleep compiles against JDK 17, which has no such package), so native-image needs every",
    "method and field it looks up registered, and the downcall's shape registered under foreign. Without these `bleep server top` cannot",
    "measure memory in the native binary. `bleep selftest` measures its own footprint, so CI fails if this falls out of step with the code."
  ],
